No `@types/ajv` installed. 34GB memory available, so a `tsc --noEmit` won't OOM here (the 1Gi constraint was for the Linux CI pod).

Now, `ErrorObject` in ajv 8 types — let me check whether `instancePath` exists. From `./types`: `interface ErrorObject<K extends string, P, S> { keyword: K; instancePath: string; schemaPath: string; params: P; ... }`. Let me verify in the installed types.

The CI errors say:
- `registry.ts(115,11): error TS2339: Property 'instancePath' does not exist on type 'ErrorObject'.`
- `registry.ts(115,31): error TS2339: ...`

Line 115: `e.instancePath ? `${e.instancePath} ${e.message}` : String(e.message)` — col 11 is `e.instancePath` first use, col 31 second use.

If ajv 8.20's ErrorObject has `instancePath: string` as required, TS2339 wouldn't fire. Unless... the ErrorObject resolved is a different one. Hmm — `import type {ValidateFunction} from 'ajv'` on line 2. ValidateFunction is `(data) => boolean; errors?: ErrorObject[]`. From './types'.

Wait... maybe the installed ajv is NOT 8.20 in CI. CI runs `npm ci` which installs per lockfile = 8.20.0. Hmm.

OK here's another thought: is there maybe ANOTHER copy of ajv in node_modules — e.g. `node_modules/ajv/dist/` vs some nested `node_modules/x/node_modules/ajv`? TS resolution from `src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts` walks up: `src/node_modules`, `node_modules` (root). Root is 8.20.0. So types come from 8.20.0's `dist/ajv.d.ts`.

Hmm hold on. Let me re-read `dist/ajv.d.ts` head — I only saw the tail. Maybe the head has something odd. Let me view the whole file. Actually the tail showed:

```ts
import type { AnySchemaObject } from "./types";
import AjvCore from "./core";
export declare class Ajv extends AjvCore {
    _addVocabularies(): void;
    _addDefaultMetaSchema(): void;
    defaultMeta(): string | AnySchemaObject | undefined;
